NAME
  apt - update Freax from the network without leaving the game

SYNOPSIS
  apt update [--source=URL]
  apt upgrade [--yes] [--force] [--source=URL]
  apt version
  apt sources

DESCRIPTION
  apt pulls core OS files over HTTP from an update source (by default
  the GitHub project) and installs them onto the running hard drive.
  No world restart is needed: files stream straight to disk in small
  chunks, half-written downloads are never left in place (temp file
  plus rename), and your accounts and config (/etc/passwd,
  /etc/shadow, /etc/hostname, custom /etc/apt/sources.list, /home)
  are never overwritten.

  Kernel and boot files take effect on the next in-game reboot, not
  instantly. apt prompts for that reboot; everything else (shell,
  tools, libs, man pages) is live for the next command you run.

  apt requires an internet card (see `man wget`).

COMMANDS
  update
    Fetch the remote VERSION and manifest, compare with the local
    /VERSION, and report. Caches the manifest for `upgrade`.
  upgrade
    Download every manifest file and install it. Prompts before
    starting unless --yes is given. Skips files already up to date
    unless --force is given.
  version
    Print the local version (works offline).
  sources
    Print the effective update source (works offline).

OPTIONS
  --source=URL
    Use URL as the update source for this run instead of
    /etc/apt/sources.list. The repo root mirrors the installed
    root (/), so apt fetches URL + path per manifest entry.
  --yes, -y
    Do not prompt before downloading (upgrade only).
  --force, -f
    Re-download even when local and remote versions match.

FILES
  /VERSION, /manifest
  /etc/apt/sources.list

EXAMPLES
  apt update
    Check for a new release.

  apt upgrade
    Install it, then reboot when asked.

  apt upgrade --source=http://192.168.1.5:8000/
    Update from a local test mirror.
